1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Toward the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Will you take a little of it, I wonder?

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,140
They laughed at me for
still being such a kid.

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, saving up,
one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water flask,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls toward the wide sky.

10
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow have to end, I wonder?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,040
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost again.

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,860
The great metropolis of Tokyo,

13
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:46,560
this city overflowing with people, people, people,
its peace and safety

14
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:50,020
are guarded day and night by hardened men.

15
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:57,300
They are the super policemen who serve
in this Special Investigation Division.

16
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,880
Kaipan Deka, also known as Detective Kitano,

17
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:06,120
is an elite detective who has solved countless
difficult cases through sheer natural talent.

18
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,040
He is the king of land.

19
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,720
Gekko Deka and Venus Deka,

20
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:19,720
transform to suit any situation and fly
through the sky in the night fighter Gekko.

21
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,840
They are the kings of the sky.

22
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,640
Dolphin Deka, the Dozaemon of the sea,

23
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,560
a former dolphin trainer who afterward

24
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:34,420
worked as a glassmaker and manga
artist before becoming a detective.

25
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,520
He is the king of the sea.

26
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,140
And this man,

27
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:47,180
who leads a team of formidable officers, is in
charge of the Special Investigation Division.

28
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,660
With a topknot and all

29
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:55,500
Yeah!

30
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:59,400
I've gathered you all here for one reason,

31
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:03,360
I want to recruit a new rookie for
our Special Investigation Division.

32
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,280
So,

33
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:09,440
I want you experienced men to name one
person you think would be a good fit.

34
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:11,720
Someone you think is a great candidate.

35
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,180
Someone who can handle the
tough work of a special detective,

36
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,320
there's only one person I can think of.

37
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:21,840
Who's that?

38
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:29,680
Episode 1: Kankichi Ryotsu of
the Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box

39
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:36,420
W-why do I have to be
stuck with you perverts in

40
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,760
the Special Investigation Division?

41
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,240
Punishment time!

42
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,720
Got something to say?

43
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,440
Here comes the punishment!

44
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:55,180
Got it! I get it, so stop!

45
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,700
Good, as long as you understand.

46
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,480
Hey ow ow.

47
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:01,762
But...

48
00:04:01,812 --> 00:04:05,820
I don't have special skills like you lot,
and I don't have a partner either!

49
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,217
Don't worry.

50
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:10,220
I've got something the boss entrusted to me.

51
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,180
A pigeon?

52
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,620
W-why would I have to deal with a pigeon!

53
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,340
It's no ordinary pigeon!

54
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:21,954
Yes.

55
00:04:22,004 --> 00:04:28,869
the super-elite battle pigeon our Special Investigation
Division trained with every ounce of passion,

56
00:04:28,919 --> 00:04:30,480
Deiemon.

57
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,273
But,

58
00:04:31,323 --> 00:04:34,740
smart as it is,
how could a pigeon be defeated?

59
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,540
I'll punish you again, Deka!

60
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:40,080
W-wait, wait, I've had enough of punishment!

61
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,120
You don't know anything at all.

62
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,340
Look at this.

63
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:48,660
Now a kamishibai has appeared.

64
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,055
Whoops, ready?

65
00:04:51,105 --> 00:04:54,900
Kamishibai always comes
with mizuame. Eat up.

66
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:56,856
Eat it, you say? Even so,

67
00:04:56,906 --> 00:05:00,040
I clearly saw you pull
that out of there just now.

68
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:03,320
The time was World War I.

69
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:08,000
Under the German army's offensive, the
French army was isolated at Verdun Fortress.

70
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,660
Radio communications were jammed, and the
underground telephone line was also cut by bombing.

71
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:17,700
The German encirclement kept closing in,

72
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:20,560
and everyone was on the verge of giving up.

73
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:27,400
Then Major Renard sent a military
pigeon off as a messenger.

74
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:34,040
Soon, French reinforcements received the
pigeon's message and rushed to the rescue.

75
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:37,520
A single pigeon saved the unit.

76
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:40,840
No matter how many times I hear it,
it's a moving story.

77
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,660
Wow, pigeons are amazing, aren't they?

78
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:47,020
Exactly, that's right.

79
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,280
Haa.

80
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:01,700
Reiko, are you pretty?

81
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,920
Is Reiko pretty?

82
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,460
Such flattery.

83
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:07,040
Well then.

84
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:10,580
What are you doing?

85
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,000
Ryo-chan.

86
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:15,620
What's this?

87
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:18,975
Listen, Ryotsu.

88
00:06:19,025 --> 00:06:22,080
From today, you're Hatopoppo Deka.

89
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:24,700
Hatopoppo Deka?!

90
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,140
No way, I won't do that.

91
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,920
Chief, you have to do something about this.

92
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,640
Ugh, I can't breathe.

93
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,840
Give up, Ryotsu.

94
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:37,700
How cold! Are you really going
to abandon your cute subordinate?

95
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,660
You're not cute.

96
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,160
Demon, devil!

97
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:44,900
No, forget I said that, please.

98
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:45,740
I don't know anything about it.

99
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,640
Hey, w-wait, what are you doing?

100
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:51,840
Everyone, withdraw!

101
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,680
No, I haven't agreed to this yet!

102
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,720
Hey, Chief, I'll hold a grudge against you!
I'll curse you!

103
00:06:57,820 --> 00:06:59,940
No matter what you say, I won't answer!

104
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,720
With this,
I can finally have hope for my future.

105
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,860
No, let go!

106
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,080
Reiko, Sakagawa, do something!

107
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:10,580
I don't want to join the ranks of perverts!

108
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,720
Good for you, Ryo-chan.

109
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,260
Good luck, senpai.

110
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,800
Damn it, are you guys even friends?

111
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,440
If I say I hate it,
then I absolutely hate it.

112
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,920
This is a tremendous honor, you know.

113
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:32,320
Besides, if you're assigned to the Special Investigation Division,
your salary doubles.

114
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,620
I refuse, no matter what you say.

115
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:36,960
What, is that really true?

116
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:40,620
Since the work is so hard,
you get a special allowance.

117
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:42,980
And the costume expenses add up, too.

118
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:45,880
Costume money?
That's just one store-bought bread roll!

119
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:49,680
As Hatopoppo Deka,
you'll be given money for pigeon feed.

120
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:52,920
You'll live as if the
pigeon were your own brother.

121
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,400
I've got a feeling I was tricked somehow.

122
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,640
Going out on patrol is fine,

123
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:15,280
but everyone at this police
box will be staring at me.

124
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:17,480
Ow

125
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,240
What the hell are you doing?

126
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,100
What, is this the fastest way to get feed?

127
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,480
No way, no way!

128
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:27,320
I still haven't been paid

129
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,880
a single yen as a Special Detective!

130
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,740
I'm not giving you any feed.

131
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,780
I'm not going easy on you.

132
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,740
Earn your own feed money.

133
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:40,540
Hey, where are you going?

134
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:45,040
What?

135
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,800
A 100-yen coin.

136
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:48,380
I see.

137
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:52,480
So it's trained to gather
up dropped items too?

138
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:55,820
Good, now go fetch more.

139
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:57,500
Do that, and I'll buy you some beans.

140
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,060
Whoo-hoo!

141
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,220
Whoo-hoo!

142
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:30,800
And so, Deiemon and I forged
a bond of fierce friendship.

143
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:36,760
It's already been a week since you were assigned
to the Special Investigation Division, senpai.

144
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:40,160
Looks like you're getting along with Deiemon after all,
Ryo-chan.

145
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:44,960
It's been so peaceful on my end this past week,
I can hardly believe it.

146
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,960
Speaking of which, work has been
going much faster since Ryo-chan left.

147
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,920
It really has.

148
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:55,720
Just you wait.

149
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:58,960
If you think I'll keep quiet like this,
you're dead wrong.

150
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,340
Well, I'm off on patrol.

151
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:06,240
Go, Deiemon!

152
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,020
I'm going to stick to the
Chief and dig up his secrets.

153
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:16,900
Now that that troublemaker is gone...

154
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:19,180
Looks like my luck has finally turned.

155
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,060
Look, 500 yen just lying here!

156
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,820
Good, good.

157
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:03,760
Yes, this is Ohara.

158
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:06,760
It's Ryotsu.

159
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,960
Have you already given up?
I won't listen to any whining.

160
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:15,840
No, Chief, I wouldn't trouble
your ears over something like that.

161
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:18,300
Then what is it? I'm busy.

162
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:24,260
Well, Chief, I was just wondering if you properly
turned in the 500 yen you found to the police box.

163
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:27,940
And I also had my trousers properly mended.

164
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:34,380
W-what are you talking about?

165
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:37,720
It's no use pretending. I know everything.

166
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:41,260
I also know the Chief has been
troubled by hair loss lately.

167
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,300
W-what? That's ridiculous!

168
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:51,380
Who was it again? That actress's photo book had nude pictures,
didn't it?

169
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:57,500
You bought it, didn't you? I wonder
what would happen if I told your wife.

170
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:01,460
Ryotsu, fine, what do you want me to do?

171
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,480
Well, for today, I'll let it slide.

172
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,120
But don't you forget it.

173
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:11,080
Wherever you go,
my watchful eyes are on you.

174
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,640
Hey, Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

175
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:18,420
How on earth did that guy...

176
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:27,600
Listen, I'll give you more feed,
so go scout the pigeons around here.

177
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,500
Got it?

178
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:32,960
Just you watch.

179
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:44,420
Nakagawa and Reiko, who laughed and waved me off when I was
assigned to the Special Investigation Division, are just as guilty.

180
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:52,340
I'll use those pigeons to
build a massive spy unit.

181
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,500
So you got a call too, Chief?

182
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,160
Did Ryotsu call you guys too?

183
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:15,160
Ryo-chan knows exactly who my
marriage meeting partner is.

184
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:20,200
He even knows the details of the
new project our company is starting.

185
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,840
How creepy.

186
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,500
It's unsettling.

187
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,000
A call from the police box?

188
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:46,600
It's complaints from the police box.

189
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:50,420
Sounds like they're griping
about me at the police box.

190
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:50,840
Good.

191
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:54,340
How on earth is he spying on us, I wonder?

192
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,680
Yes, this is Kameari Park police box.

193
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:08,240
Looks like you were talking about me.

194
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,080
Senpai!

195
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:10,140
W-what?

196
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,700
I'm not nearby.

197
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:17,300
Even from a distance, I see everything.

198
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:18,360
Senpai!

199
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:22,060
Come out, Ryo-chan, that's cowardly!

200
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:22,970
No way,

201
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:27,180
I'll keep exposing your private lives,
so consider yourselves warned.

202
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,120
Hey, Ryo-chan, Ryo-chan!

203
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:32,540
Damn you, Ryotsu.

204
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:46,820
W-what is this?!
Why are there so many pigeons here?!

205
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:49,035
It's creepy, isn't it.
Apparently that caveman,

206
00:14:49,085 --> 00:14:52,700
ever since Kankichi Ryotsu became Hatopoppo Deka,
that's what happened.

207
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:56,500
Honestly, that guy.
He causes nothing but trouble for everyone!

208
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,540
What are you doing,
you sexual harassment pigeon?

209
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,720
What is this flock of pigeons?

210
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,160
It's the senior officer's doing.

211
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:13,680
What?

212
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:19,660
So Ryotsu is using the pigeons to spy on us?

213
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:21,320
That's the only explanation I can think of.

214
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,880
He also knows the parents'
private affairs suspiciously well.

215
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,260
Apparently, whenever you turn around,
there's a pigeon right beside him.

216
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:26,991
That reminds me,

217
00:15:27,041 --> 00:15:30,300
There was even a time pigeons
chased after my Ferrari.

218
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:34,920
Grr, that Ryotsu, taking advantage
of becoming a Hatopoppo Deka...

219
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,940
Chief.

220
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:39,200
Yeah.

221
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:45,640
If you talk badly about Ryo-chan,
you'll get payback right away.

222
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:55,080
They've really multiplied.

223
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:56,860
Papa's here.

224
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,000
What, you want even more?

225
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,540
Don't be greedy!
The feed costs add up, you know!

226
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:10,100
All you ever bring in is pocket change!

227
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:13,740
If you've got complaints,
then go out and earn me some big money!

228
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:25,600
So he can even use a PC?

229
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:28,900
What?

230
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,180
Race 7, top pick: Kikao.

231
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,140
Gerry.

232
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:37,200
Is this for real?

233
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:41,340
So that means a single bet on the second favorite,
Meguro Sanma?

234
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:45,600
You've got more info, don't you? Spill it.

235
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,920
Fine, let's increase the amount of feed.

236
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:55,100
I'll get them top-grade beans from Hokkaido.

237
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:02,200
Let's see...
Yamada Nishiki is in fantastic form!

238
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:05,400
Alright, let's go with the third-place pick,
Yamada Nishiki.

239
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,980
And here comes Yamada
Nishiki from the outside!

240
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:09,900
Kicker Ōmeguro isn't pulling ahead either.

241
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,880
Yamada Diary:
Yamada Diary is coming through!

242
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,740
Yamada Diary:
crossing the finish line in first place!

243
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,040
Yes!

244
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:19,020
Three hundred thousand yen, jackpot!

245
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:26,220
With all those Sundays,
I've made a million from the long shots!

246
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:32,440
No matter how many times I look at it,
it's still great.

247
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,580
This texture.

248
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:38,620
This feeling.

249
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:48,460
With this million as my stake,
I'll go all in on a big bet.

250
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:49,740
Thief!

251
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:50,460
What?

252
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,180
Give it back!

253
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:54,620
What happened? What was taken?

254
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:58,160
That case has 100 million yen in cash in it!

255
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,580
What? 100 million yen?

256
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,100
Why were you carrying
around that much money?

257
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:07,740
I only trust cash deals, that's my policy.

258
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:10,160
If you catch him, I'll pay you 10%.

259
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,120
Of course, in cash.

260
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:15,840
10 million?

261
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,260
Right! Leave it to me!

262
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,420
Go, Tenimon!
Chase him to the ends of the earth!

263
00:18:26,780 --> 00:18:29,520
Don't think you can escape Hatopoppo Teka!

264
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:33,620
No. I got carried away without realizing it.

265
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:40,680
What's going on, what's going on!

266
00:18:58,420 --> 00:18:59,840
What an amazing guy!

267
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:01,060
You!

268
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:03,280
Take this!

269
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:10,800
Zabaamiro!

270
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,560
Can you follow me this far?

271
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:13,540
Damn it!

272
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:15,180
Letting him get away like that!

273
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:17,080
What are you doing?

274
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,260
With pigeons

275
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,540
And you call yourselves the police?

276
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:21,880
Ignoring me again!

277
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,540
The army

278
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:24,960
The air force

279
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:32,480
Protect... and Papa, too? What you're
guarding is the Rikutora room. Got it?

280
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,700
Denemon! Hey! Denemon!

281
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,820
Round up your buddies! It's a big payout!

282
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:57,100
Yeah! Here, here!

283
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:01,640
I'll do anything for 10% of 100 million yen,
that's 10 million!

284
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:08,060
This is comfortable.

285
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:13,460
My 10 million! No,
the 100 million yen you stole! Give it back!

286
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,520
And don't think you can escape the pigeons!

287
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:18,040
W-what was that?

288
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,320
Go! Don't let him escape!

289
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,540
Go! Don't let him escape!

290
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,500
Please be careful.
The express train is now departing.

291
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,220
Stop!

292
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:47,340
What a persistent bastard.

293
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:00,820
Wait!

294
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:01,360
You bastard!

295
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:06,600
Hey!

296
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:19,520
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

297
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,580
I thought I was going to die!

298
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:23,760
Wait, wait, wait!

299
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,440
How far are you going to keep chasing me?!

300
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:30,160
Give me back my 10 million yen!

301
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,000
Get closer!
Closer and closer, don't slow down!

302
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,600
Closer, closer!

303
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,280
I'm not letting you get away anymore!

304
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,960
Even if you come closer,
we're up in the sky!

305
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,920
You can't touch me any further!

306
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,480
But where do you think you're going?

307
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:47,640
He's the kind of man who never comes to
buy the limited-edition explosive blade.

308
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:51,300
I'm riding solo!

309
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,560
Stop! Hand over that bag, now!

310
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:54,840
W-where's the thief?

311
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:55,900
Which way did the thief go?

312
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:56,660
What?

313
00:22:01,672 --> 00:22:07,660
It's 100 million yen!

314
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,280
The stolen 100 million yen! Gather it up!

315
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:34,220


316
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,980
D-Denemon, do something!

317
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:47,680
Yes, good! Bring that back here!

318
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:53,056
Hey! My 1 million yen,

319
00:22:53,106 --> 00:22:55,440
don't you dare pocket it!

320
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:58,457
Hey, you lot!
If you find it, every last one of you,

321
00:22:58,507 --> 00:23:00,800
I'll make you into 100 tons
of tsukudani and eat you!

322
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:02,080
You'll pay for this!

323
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:23,180
A pigeon that buys its own feed appears!

324
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:27,680
The money this pigeon is using is your 1 million yen,
senpai, right?

325
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:31,660
Even the pigeons have given up on him.
He's really a hopeless case.

326
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:36,520
Poppo, and hato-poppo too!

327
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:41,960
You want beans? Here, take some!

328
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:47,740
Let's all go eat together, nicely.

329
00:23:47,740 --> 00:23:52,100
This time it was a failure

330
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:55,240
The idea of
"Hato-Poppo Deka" was good, though.

331
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,880
Let's look forward to next time.

332
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:57,440
Yeah.

333
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:01,740
Well then, see you again in the
next Special Detective series!

334
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:08,460
Stop saying
"sorry, sorry" over and over. It's really annoying.

335
00:24:08,460 --> 00:24:12,600
Name? Your name is Sumimasen Taro?

336
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:17,060
No wonder you've spent your whole life causing
trouble for people with a name like that.

337
00:24:17,060 --> 00:24:21,620
Next time: Today, Kami wa Nagai Tomodachi.
See you then.

338
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,020
No, no, and it's solved!

339
00:24:41,020 --> 00:24:42,680
Please, please, quickly!

340
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:44,040
Whoa, and lending a hand!

341
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:45,620
Prediction.

342
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:48,360
Decided, net-style,

343
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,900
and a flash of inspiration!

344
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:51,340
Bouncing along,

345
00:24:51,340 --> 00:24:52,740
and wrapping it all up!

346
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:54,240
And into action!

347
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,700
And off they fly!

348
00:24:56,700 --> 00:25:00,380
Above all, power for sumo!

349
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:02,820
Everyone, gather!

350
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:06,400
Come here,

351
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:12,740
the dreamlike final energy!

352
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:16,620
Gazing at tomorrow, your star,

353
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:20,040
paint the whole Earth,
and stand on the ground!

354
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,800
The Kameari star spins
round and returns the ring!

355
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,480
This should be fine, right?

356
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,960
Like hell it is!

357
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,760
Thanks for watching!

